        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            The specification that works on almost any block wall is the same one professionals use: fix the moisture, let the wall cure and dry, apply a proper masonry block filler, then two coats of 100 per cent acrylic masonry paint. Skip any of those and the wall tells on you within two years.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            If the block is damp and you cannot resolve why, stop before you paint. A coating over active moisture does not solve anything — it relocates the failure to somewhere less visible and considerably more expensive.
          </p>
        </div>

